## 4. Phase 4 — Quality Gates (must pass before presenting output)

Before showing generated files to the user, verify:

- [ ] Every endpoint path / selector / field name in generated tests matches
      something actually read in Phase 1 — grep the source artifact to
      confirm, don't trust memory of the analysis.
- [ ] No `TODO`, `FIXME`, empty step body, or placeholder assertion
      (`expect(true).toBe(true)`-style) anywhere in generated output.
- [ ] No literal secret, token, or hardcoded environment URL — all sourced
      from env vars matching the repo's existing convention.
- [ ] Every flow has at least one negative/edge case, not just happy path.
- [ ] Dependency versions added match the repo's existing version scheme
      (checked against lockfile/BOM, not assumed).
- [ ] Generated files land in the directory convention detected/confirmed
      in 1.5, not an arbitrary new location.
- [ ] If this is a re-run, no existing test file was overwritten without
      explicit confirmation (Section 7.5).

If any box fails, fix it before presenting — do not present partial or
placeholder output and label it done.

